  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Capacities for Protection of Ukrainian Refugees, Third Country Nationals and Host Communities in the Republic of Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 24February 2022, the Russian Federation launched a broad military offensive against Ukraine. The situation quickly deteriorated, with major attacks being reported across the country, including in the capital, Kyiv. Immediately after the attacks began, a spike in migratory flows was observed from Ukraine into neighbouring countries, including the Republic of Moldova. This high influx of refugees and Third Country Nationals (TCNs) brings an unprecedented situation for the Republic of Moldova, a country of only 2.5 million people and an economy already heavily impacted by two years of the COVID-19 pandemic. Through this project, IOM is seeling to strengthen the protection response in Moldova, by providing assistance and building capacities of local and national authorities so the needs of the most vulnerable are met, particularly women, children, older persons, minority groups and persons living with disabilities. Protection programming aims to restore the dignity and rights of those who have experienced violence such as gender-based violence (GBV) survivors and persons with disabilities. IOM also recognizes the need to establish adequate response mechanisms and strengthen an integrated approach to border management to ultimately facilitate, assist, and protect conflict-affected populations crossing borders and ensure safe pathways are guaranteed by rights-based policies and procedures.</narrative>
  </description>
